Dear Robert,

Please be advised that QSCP-NCR-2024-031 and QSCP-NCR-2024-032 are now officially closed for the ATU-100. These nonconformances were originally issued following the discovery of wall loss below t-min at CML 4-RA-101-06 and across the 2-RF-102 reflux line.

During the QSCP Turnaround 2026, replacement spools were installed on both 4-RA-101 and 2-RF-102. We have verified the new-spool baseline data provided in LNDE-RPT-20260803-034-R0, which confirms the 304L CMLs were measured at the correct stainless velocity setting. The Inspection Data Management System has been updated to reflect these new thicknesses and the reset corrosion rates.

Best regards,  Jennifer Walsh Inspection Coordinator, API 570 inspector QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department  To: Robert Hendricks Unit Engineer ATU-100, P.Eng.

